      "message": "\u003e Do you know where we\u0027re calling the bare version of clang?\n\nIn Zephyr CMake files, [here](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/91a1e706535b2f99433280513c5bc66dfb918506/cmake/compiler/clang/target.cmake#L46) for example.\n\nThis is a bit complicated. Clang is a native cross compiler and Zephyr knows it. Zephyr doesn\u0027t support prefixes (`CROSS_COMPILE` variable) for LLVM. It will just call `clang --target TRIPLE` and this is more/less equivalent to calling `armv7m-cros-eabi-clang`. `strace -f armv7m-cros-eabi-clang` finally passes control to `/usr/bin/clang`:\n\n```\n$ strace -f armv7m-cros-eabi-clang\n...\nexecve(\"/usr/bin/clang\", [\"/usr/bin/clang\", \"--sysroot\u003d/usr/armv7m-cros-eabi\", \"-L/usr/armv7m-cros-eabi/usr/lib\", \"-Qunused-arguments\", \"-Werror\u003dpoison-system-directorie\"..., \"-Wno-deprecated-declarations\", \"-Wno-enum-constexpr-conversion\", \"-Wno-error\u003dimplicit-function-dec\"..., \"-Wno-error\u003dimplicit-int\", \"-Wno-unknown-warning-option\", \"-fdebug-default-version\u003d5\", \"-Wno-int-conversion\", \"-Wno-incompatible-function-point\"..., \"-Wno-error\u003dvla-cxx-extension\", \"-D_LIBCPP_ENABLE_CXX17_REMOVED_F\"..., \"-Wno-section\", \"-static-libgcc\", \"--prefix\u003d../../../../../../usr/l\"..., \"-B../../../../../../usr/libexec/\"..., \"-target\", \"armv7m-cros-eabi\"], 0x556ae763ff90 /* 49 vars */) \u003d 0\n...\n```\n\nZephyr only calls `clang` to find path to compiler headers and path to compiler-rt library. This is okay because `/usr/bin/clang` and `armv7m-cros-eabi-clang` are the same compiler, so paths are the same.\n\nLater we change the compiler to `armv7m-cros-eabi-clang` in our CMake scripts, so source files are compiled using wrapper.\n\n\u003e I think what Rack was referring to in http://b/360183429#comment16 is that we shouldn\u0027t be calling \"bare\" clang anywhere (i.e., clang) and should only be calling the prefixed version (armv7m-cros-eabi-clang).\n\nThere are two `clang` compilers really. The first is a \"board\" compiler (used to compile ebuilds) and the second compiler is our `armv7m-cros-eabi-clang` (`/usr/bin/clang` + arguments actually). As a result of Rack change, we call the \"board\" compiler.\n\n\u003e There shouldn\u0027t be anything wrong with calling `clang --target TRIPLE`\n\nYes. I agree. Calling clang using `clang --target TRIPLE` should be the preferred way. I understand that toolchain team provided wrapper to be compatible with GCC though.\n\n\u003e IIUC, the other method that was suggested was to add a --toolchain argument to zmake in the ebuild.\n\nIt won\u0027t work. `--toolchain` argument only forces zmake to use LLVM, but actually zmake tries to use LLVM so it\u0027s not a problem. The problem is that Zephyr finds \"board\" clang instead of `/usr/bin/clang` aka \u0027our\u0027 clang.",
